You can install and verify mitmproxy (which provides mitmproxy, mitmdump, and mitmweb) on Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) using pipx so you get the latest release cleanly isolated from system Python packages.

1. One-Command Installation

bash
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y pipx && \
pipx ensurepath && \
pipx install mitmproxy
Use code with caution.

2. Verify All Three Binaries Are Installed & Ready

bash
export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"

for tool in mitmproxy mitmdump mitmweb; do
  if command -v "$tool" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "✅ $tool -> $(command -v "$tool")"
  else
    echo "❌ $tool -> MISSING"
  fi
done

mitmproxy --version | head -n 2
Use code with caution.
(Note: After launching mitmproxy or mitmdump once, its root CA certificate is automatically generated in ~/.mitmproxy/mitmproxy-ca-cert.pem for intercepting HTTPS traffic.)
